ethercat (1:1.7.0~rc1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First downstream 1.7 release candidate, based on EtherLab stable-1.7.
  * Retain the parallel per-slave scan/configuration and AL recovery work.
  * Include Linux 6.18 and Clang build fixes.
  * Add SII read/write APIs and refresh the SII image after writes, including
    invalidation of the 1.7 SII page cache.
  * Add opt-in ReinitHold so applications can restore volatile slave
    configuration after reconnection before the slave returns to OP.
  * Update the library ABI and document the application restoration workflow.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:45:44 +0800

ethercat (1.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase on official stable-1.7 (SII cache, PDO mode, ioctl 43).
  * Keep parallel per-slave scan/config and AL recovery from 1.6.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:50:00 -0400

ethercat (1.6.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sync official stable-1.6 through 1.6.13 (drivers, FoE/EoE hardening,
    datagram re-order barriers, max-frame split).
  * Keep our parallel slave scan/config, AL recovery and DC patches.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:40:00 -0400

ethercat (1.6.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Parallel slave configuration (multi-slave bus reaches OP in seconds).
  * SDO information API and bus rescan in the realtime library.
  * Numerous stability fixes (datagram index reuse, external-ring timing,
    mailbox state machines, SDO dictionary gating, DC sync1 shift).
  * SII timing relaxed for slow EEPROMs.
  * New ethercat diag command, slave port bypass detection and upstream
    port inference.
  * FoE password support.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
